# Explain codes inline

The user gets confused between corpus identifiers, spec-kit labels and pipeline names.
Whenever a message to the user mentions a code, add a short explanation in parentheses
right after it, every time, not just the first time.

Covers:
- Spec-kit labels: task IDs, user stories, requirement and success-criteria IDs
- Pipeline names: dataset versions, permission groups, test users
- Corpus identifiers: procedure names, asset IDs, fault codes, parameters, case and work order numbers, model names

Examples:
- T045 (task: similarity check for restricted procedures)
- US2 (user story: service history per machine)
- FR-008 (requirement: every page has content or a recorded reason)
- ds_0007 (dataset version 7)
- u03 (test technician without high-voltage certification)
- cert-hv (permission group: high-voltage certified)
- HV-PROC-07 (high-voltage repair procedure, restricted)
- P9.01 (drive parameter in HV-PROC-07)
- TP1 (test point in HV-PROC-07)
- E-31 (compressor fault code)
- TAC-C-0142 (a machine's asset ID)
- 00041207 (Salesforce support case)
- 2501292 (Servio work order)
